{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789906693,"nonce":"F82/nhy0V+G/p2RsDjFqvYKc6to=","title":"Cranelift prologue mapped parameter values by position, not by index","message":"The prologue of a compiled function collected the HIR values of kind\nParameter(n), sorted them by n and zipped them with the block\nparameters. A pass that deletes the value of a parameter nothing reads\n(dead value removal after CSE or DCE does) leaves a gap in the\nsequence, and every parameter after the gap was mapped one place too\nearly: it read the previous parameter's register.\n\nSeen on an outlined resume point of nbody's advance: 66 parameters, the\nvalues of indices 48 and 64 gone after optimisation, the Cranelift\nverifier rejecting an icmp on an f64 that was meant to be an i64. A\nplain function with an unused parameter followed by used ones would\nhit the same when the optimiser dropped the unused value; the lowering\nkeeps parameter values alive for the ordinary path, which is why it\nnever showed.\n\nFix: map each remaining Parameter(n) value to block parameter n.","files":null}]}